  <data name="Info_RepositorySummary_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Summary of the repository</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositorySummary_What" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Here you see how the project folder is: its branch, whether it has unsaved changes and where it is published. It is only read: nothing is changed here.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositorySummary_Actions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>See which branch you are on and which is the latest saved version.
Check whether there are unsaved changes.
Review the remotes: the places where the repository is published.
Press "Refresh" to read it again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryBranches_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Branches of the repository</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryBranches_What" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Branches are lines of work of the repository. Here are yours and those Agent Studio creates for each run.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryBranches_Actions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Look for the current branch: it has a mark.
Recognize the branches of a run: they say they are from Agent Studio.
See which saved version each one points to.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryCommits_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Saved versions</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryCommits_What" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Each saved version (commit) is a point in the history of the project. If Agent Studio made it, it says the run, the task, the attempt, the agent and the model. It only says so if the log backs it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryCommits_Actions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>See who made each version and when.
Look at the suggestions: they are marked and they are not certain.
If it is available, open the chain of a version: its requirement, its proof and its verdict.
Press "Refresh" to read the history again.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryActivity_Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Activity of the repository</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryActivity_What" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Here is what happened in the repository: the integrations, the deliveries and the working copies that were removed. Each line says whether it worked or why it failed.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Info_RepositoryActivity_Actions" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Filter by run, task, milestone, agent, provider or model.
Pick a period to see only what is recent.
See the real result of each integration or delivery.
Clear the filters to see everything.</value>
  </data>
